.TH SQLITE3 2
.SH NAME
sqlite3 \- native SQLite library and Plan 9 file interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
#include <u.h>
#include <libc.h>
#include <sqlite3.h>
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Libsqlite3
provides the SQLite C API with a native VFS named
.BR plan9 .
The header selects the library. Compile clients with
.BR -p .
The SQL language, C interfaces and database format follow upstream SQLite.
.PP
The VFS opens database files with
.BR DMEXCL .
Exclusivity lasts until the connection closes, including between transactions;
read-only connections also exclude other connections.
The SQLite lock callbacks record the pager's logical lock state within this
stronger file lock.
A competing open fails; retry opening after the owner closes.
SQLite busy timeouts do not retry failed opens.
.PP
New databases are created exclusively with mode
.BR DMEXCL|0666 .
Existing mutable databases must already have
.B DMEXCL
set. An ordinary file is rejected without changing its contents or mode.
The VFS uses positioned I/O, length changes through
.IR stat (2),
and
.B ORCLOSE
for temporary files in
.BR /tmp .
.PP
Synchronization sends an empty
.B wstat
to the file; journal deletion also synchronizes the parent directory.
The server must hold exclusive opens until clunk and implement the stable-storage
meaning of empty wstat described in
.IR stat (5).
No atomic-write or powersafe-overwrite properties are assumed.
.PP
.I Gefs
and
.I ramfs
provide lifetime exclusive opens; ramfs data is volatile.
.I U9fs
does not provide the required semantics and rejects database creation.
Servers that expire exclusive-use locks, such as
.IR cwfs ,
are unsupported: loss of the database lock cannot fence writes to its journal.
Durability still depends on the server and its backing storage.
.PP
An explicit
.B immutable=1
URI opens a read-only snapshot without requiring DMEXCL.
The caller must ensure that no process changes the file while it is open.
Do not rename, replace, remove, or clear DMEXCL on an open database.
Keep the database and its adjacent journals together in the namespace.
Copy databases between systems only after closing their connections.
.PP
The build has no internal mutexes; callers must serialize access to SQLite
state. Do not use inherited connections after fork.
Initialization disables floating-point traps for SQLite's IEEE arithmetic.
WAL, memory mapping, loadable extensions and the localtime date modifier
are omitted. Rollback journals, JSON and UTC date functions are available.
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/libsqlite3
